// Lensowl: an owl astronomer perched at the back of a brass telescope rover, a clockwork moon
// hovering over it. Its cutout rig: the art only.
//
// World pixels. Body frame: origin = the center of the ground contact between the wheels, +x =
// facing, +y = down; facing left mirrors x. Every part SVG puts its pivot at its own origin, so
// `at` is where that pivot lands in the body frame, and `cargo xtask art` renders each part with
// its pivot at the image's center (lobshot_assets::ART_SCALE pixels per world pixel).
//
// Gameplay geometry (hitbox, ground probes, aim range, cannon pivot and barrel length) lives in
// sim::tuning::lensowl; `cargo xtask art` refuses a rig whose cannon disagrees with it.
MobileRig(
    name: "Lensowl",
    parts: [
        // Drawn in z order, lowest first. spin: rolls as it moves; aim: turns with the cannon.
        // The wheels sit under the hull.
        (id: "wheel_rear",  file: "wheel.svg",  at: (-21.0, -8.4), z: 1, spin: true),
        (id: "wheel_front", file: "wheel.svg",  at: (21.0, -8.4),  z: 1, spin: true),
        (id: "body",        file: "body.svg",   at: (0.0, 0.0),    z: 2),
        // The telescope turns on the trunnion atop its mount post, at the front of the deck.
        (id: "cannon",      file: "cannon.svg", at: (17.0, -36.0), z: 5, aim: true),
    ],
    cannon: (
        part: "cannon",
        // Where shots leave, in the cannon's frame at aim 0 (pointing +x): the objective lens, one
        // barrel length (sim::tuning) from the pivot.
        muzzle: (30.0, 0.0),
    ),
    // Riders are cosmetic and swappable; a rider's origin is its seat. The rider sits on the stool
    // in front of the owl, at the telescope's eyepiece.
    rider_socket: (at: (5.0, -27.6), z: 4),
    // The clockwork moon: drawn over the rover where sim::tuning::lensowl puts it, never leaning.
    satellite: Some("satellite.svg"),
)
